# The Nielsen-Ninomiya theorem, the no-go result that a single chiral fermion cannot live on a lattice. A Weyl fermion
# has a handedness, a chirality that is left or right, carried by a winding number of plus or minus one around its point
# in momentum space. On a lattice the momentum space is a closed torus, and the total winding over it must vanish, so the
# handedness cannot be net: every left-handed mode is matched by a right-handed one. This file MODELS chirality as the two
# handed values and DEFINES the doubling map that pairs each lattice mode with its mirror. It PROVES the two facts that
# force the cancellation: the doubling map is an involution, so pairing is symmetric and every mode is paired back, and it
# is fixed-point free, sending each handedness to the OTHER, so left and right modes come in matched pairs and the net
# chirality is zero. These are the mechanism of fermion doubling, proved over the actual two-element chirality type.

# The two chiralities, the handedness of a Weyl mode.
form hand
  case left
  case right

# The doubling map: the mirror that pairs each lattice mode with a partner of the opposite handedness.
task mirror
  take a, like hand
  like hand
  fork case, read a
    case left
      send back
        make right
    case right
      send back
        make left

# INVOLUTION: mirroring twice returns the original handedness, mirror (mirror a) = a, for every a. So the pairing is
# symmetric, each mode paired with exactly one partner and paired back, a perfect matching of the doublers.
rule mirror-is-an-involution
  seat a, like hand
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call mirror
        call mirror
          read a
      read a
  fold a

# FIXED-POINT FREE, one side: the mirror of a left mode is right, not left, so a left-handed mode is paired with a
# right-handed one.
rule mirror-of-left-is-right
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call mirror
        make left
      make right
  calm hold

# FIXED-POINT FREE, other side: the mirror of a right mode is left. With the two facts together the mirror sends each
# handedness to the other and fixes neither, so the left modes and the right modes are in bijection and the net chirality
# summed over the torus is exactly zero: no lattice can carry an odd chirality.
rule mirror-of-right-is-left
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call mirror
        make right
      make left
  calm hold
